# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 032
# Act: SIG+  (Signal aimed at Figure)   Stance: Binding   Site: Entity
#
# Binding the actual sign, on two specific entities, checked directly
# against the committed magnitude grounds rather than asserted:
#
#   kernel/data/magnitude-ground-c.json:
#     candidate 97, ground built from the other 31 values (Q25 -0.53,
#     Q75 0.475, aperture 1.005), 96.04 aperture-widths beyond Q75.
#     -> sign: "anomalous"
#
#   kernel/data/magnitude-ground-control.json:
#     candidate -0.46, ground from noise-control's other 31 values
#     (Q25 -0.555, Q75 0.36, aperture 0.915), -0.10 aperture-widths —
#     INSIDE the ground's own bounds, not beyond them.
#     -> sign: "ordinary"
#
# This is a NEW sign vocabulary ("anomalous"/"ordinary"), not a revision of
# turn-004's ("absent"/"present") — the two questions are different
# (existence vs. degree), and turn-31 named them as different classes on
# purpose. Both signs are mechanically derived from the committed ground
# computations, never re-decided by SIG, the same discipline turn-004 held.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-31 (a class to bind within) and
# the two committed magnitude-ground files (the mechanism, already run).
# Refuted if either sign disagreed with its file's own
# `aperture_widths_beyond_ground` value — checked directly above.

:turn-32  eot:opens        :turn-31 .
:turn-32  eot:act          eot:SIG+ .
:turn-32  eot:stance       "Binding" .
:turn-32  eot:site         "Entity" .
:turn-32  eot:binds        [ eot:evidence "kernel/data/magnitude-ground-c.json"       ; eot:sign "anomalous" ; eot:widths 96.04 ] .
:turn-32  eot:binds        [ eot:evidence "kernel/data/magnitude-ground-control.json" ; eot:sign "ordinary"  ; eot:widths -0.10 ] .
:turn-32  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
